themes.prompt:
Use case: stylized-concept.
Asset type: transparent motif atlas for a seamless MOTD Android chat wallpaper.

Theme: Linux, playful free-software and late-night terminal culture, with friendly
mascots and recognizable Linux symbols.

Create a precise 4 by 4 atlas of exactly 16 SEPARATE COMPLETE motifs, one intact
recognizable motif per cell, in reading order:
01 seated Tux penguin;
02 GNU mascot head;
03 Debian swirl rendered as an outlined ribbon;
04 Arch Linux emblem rendered as an outline;
05 Ubuntu Circle of Friends rendered as outlines;
06 openSUSE gecko;
07 Xfce mouse;
08 terminal window displaying exactly "$ sudo";
09 chunky keyboard with one key marked exactly "Esc";
10 package carton marked exactly ".deb";
11 package carton marked exactly ".rpm";
12 bootable USB stick with a tiny outlined penguin emblem;
13 manual booklet titled exactly "man";
14 branching filesystem tree rooted at exactly "/";
15 small kernel gear with a penguin face in its center;
16 terminal window displaying exactly "/motd".

Keep mascots expressive and recognizable. Adapt traditionally solid symbols into
outlined shapes. Tux's body must remain transparent inside its outlines, not a solid
black silhouette.

Style: playful hand-drawn crisp thin rounded MONOCHROME BLACK OUTLINE doodles, legible
at phone size, varied silhouettes, sparse internal detail, no heavy solid masses.

Each motif centered in its evenly spaced cell with at least 15 percent genuinely
transparent margin on EVERY side. Keep every contour complete and wholly inside its
cell, including tails, horns, branches, and lettering.

Actual transparent RGBA background, gutters, and outlined interiors; BLACK INK ONLY.
No white fills, opaque background, checkerboard pixels, paper, texture, shadows,
shading, gradients, color, grid lines, cell borders, numbered labels, watermark, UI
mockup, overlap, clipping, or art touching cell boundaries. Text only where explicitly
specified above; spell every string exactly.

Output only the isolated motif atlas. Do not pack a dense wallpaper or attempt
seamless edge wrapping; a deterministic compositor will do that.

Use case: stylized-concept.
Asset type: transparent motif atlas for a seamless MOTD Android chat wallpaper.
Edit the existing System Crafters motif atlas into a SIMPLER new study with ONLY SEVEN subject types. Image1 is the old atlas for outline drawing STYLE and the logos only; replace every other old subject. Image2 is the authentic System Crafters logo; use ONLY its standalone half-gear and staggered horizontal-block emblem, no wordmark. Image3 is the authentic Emacs logo; use its recognizable flowing ribbon inside a thin circle. Image4 is the authentic Guix logo; use ONLY its paired curved horns meeting in a V, no Guix wordmark.
Create a precise FOUR BY FOUR atlas of exactly16 separate complete drawings, one per equally spaced cell. Variants below are repeated instances of the SAME subject, with only very slight natural hand-drawn contour variation; preserve authentic logos.
Exact reading order:
01 standalone System Crafters half-gear and horizontal-block emblem;
02 Emacs flowing ribbon emblem within a thin circle, ribbon as thin contour with transparent interior;
03 plain standalone monospace text exactly "#systemcrafters";
04 plain balanced parentheses "()";
05 simple lambda symbol "λ";
06 plain standalone monospace text exactly "M-x", NO keyboard, keycap, frame or bubble;
07 standalone Guix paired horns/V emblem, thin outline and transparent interior;
08 second faithful System Crafters emblem, same identity, slight hand-drawn variation;
09 second faithful Emacs emblem in circle, same identity;
10 second standalone monospace "#systemcrafters";
11 second pair of parentheses "()";
12 second lambda "λ";
13 second standalone monospace "M-x", no objects;
14 second Guix horns/V emblem, same geometry;
15 third faithful System Crafters emblem;
16 third faithful Emacs emblem in circle.
The final wallpaper will have LARGE System Crafters emblems, noticeably SMALLER Emacs emblems, and MUCH SMALLER fillers. The compositor controls that scale hierarchy: for this ATLAS, draw all cells large enough to inspect, with plenty of transparent margin.
Style: playful hand-drawn crisp thin rounded MONOCHROME BLACK OUTLINE doodles. Distinctive authentic emblem geometry, legible programmer monospace lettering with equal-width glyphs. Do not draw generic substitute gears, letter E or generic bull heads. No heavy solid filled masses. Emacs ribbon and Guix horns must be OUTLINED, not solid silhouettes.
Center each complete drawing in its cell. Each drawing occupies at most60percent of cell width and height, with at least20percent truly transparent margin on EVERY side. Preserve all contours and text completely.
Actual transparent RGBA background, gutters AND outlined interiors; BLACK INK ONLY. No white fills, opaque background, checkerboard pixels, paper, texture, shadows, shading, gradients, color, grid lines, cell borders, numbered labels, watermark, UI mockup, overlap, clipping or drawing touching cell boundaries.
ONLY the seven subject types listed. Remove ALL boats, Greek shore buildings, Marvin2 tags, broken USB, keyboards, terminals, files, cons diagrams, trees, Scheme expressions, stars, hearts and other accents.
Output only the isolated complete 4x4 transparent atlas, not a finished repeat.

